

Visualizing Solutions
    
    Plot x, y, z positions over T 3d plot -> this is the reference solution
    Plot x, y, z position of the NN -> predicted solution static plot
    Plot the NN that is predicting that solution x, y, z -> predicted solution Check if we can plot for certain number of time steps
    Plot the errors between the reference solution and the predicted solution log scale
    Plot the total loss and each of the terms in the total loss
    every time you through each step of Gradient Descent plot the total loss, physics loss, and the data loss only plot at the minima
    
